kaiwa-data: language data for Kaiwa (https://github.com/shrippen/kaiwa-data)

The database kaiwa-dict.sqlite is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (CC BY-SA 4.0, see LICENSE-DATA).
It is derived from:

- JMdict, the Japanese-Multilingual Dictionary, JMnedict (Japanese names) and KANJIDIC2.
  These files are the property of the Electronic Dictionary Research and
  Development Group (EDRDG) and are used in conformance with the Group's licence.
  https://www.edrdg.org/edrdg/licence.html
  Of JMdict only the English and German glosses are included; the German glosses
  come from the JMdict German translations.

- JLPT vocabulary lists N5 to N1 by Jonathan Waller, tanos.co.uk,
  https://www.tanos.co.uk/jlpt/, licensed CC BY (Creative Commons Attribution);
  taken from snapshots in the Internet Archive (2020). Only word, reading and level
  are included. These lists are an estimate and not official JLPT lists.

- Kanjium pitch accent data (accents.txt) by Uros Ozvatic,
  https://github.com/mifunetoshiro/kanjium, CC BY-SA 4.0; partly derived from
  EDRDG data.

Changes: the sources were converted to SQLite, reduced to the fields Kaiwa uses
(see README.md), and full-width digits in accent entries were normalised (NFKC).
The date of each source is stored in the table `source` of the database.

The build scripts (build.py, fetch.sh, package.sh, tests) are MIT licensed (LICENSE).
